1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:05,500
Gliana AI Pay per result, over x402 on Algorand.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:24,480
Every generative AI provider sells by the month, to people with accounts. That suits a daily user. It fits no software agent at all, because an agent cannot fill in a signup form or hold a card on file.

3
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:39,680
So we removed the account. You ask for one model run, with no key and no signup, and the answer is a 402 that names its own price.

4
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:55,200
The challenge is the price list. The exact amount, the asset, and the address it goes to, all quoted before anything runs. This one costs a tenth of a cent in USDC

5
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:14,480
It is gasless on purpose. The facilitator's fee payer funds the group, so the buyer holds USDC and needs no ALGO at all. That is what lets an agent carry a single asset and still transact.

6
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:24,560
Paying is one command. The client signs an asset transfer group and retries the request.

7
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:36,000
Settlement confirms first, and only then is the output released. A settle failure never gives the result away for free.

8
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:49,360
Here it is on MainNet. A real USDC transfer to the payTo address, and look at the fee: zero, paid by the facilitator.

9
00:01:52,560 --> 00:02:01,600
The money moved by exactly the quoted amount. One thousand micro USDC In, one tenth of a cent.

10
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:17,760
We build the payment requirements, never the buyer. The facilitator decodes the signed group against our amount and our payTo, so a buyer cannot quote themselves a cheaper price or redirect the payment.

11
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:30,160
And we validate before charging. A request that cannot succeed is refused at the 402, not charged and then failed.

12
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:45,200
Forty-seven resources share one payTo. Image, video, music, speech, chat, and fifty utility tools, every one priced per call on Algorand MainNet.

13
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:53,360
It is live now. The code is public, and so is every endpoint.
